<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Obafemi Awolowo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1909–1987</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Obafemi Awolowo was a Nigerian lawyer and politician, the leader of the Action Group and the first premier of the Western Region from 1954 to 1959. His government introduced free primary education and other social programmes in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> west. Jailed for treasonable felony in 1963, he was released in 1966 and served as federal finance commissioner during the Nigerian Civil War, later running unsuccessfully for president in 1979 and 1983.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/obafemi-awolowo.jpg" alt="Obafemi Awolowo" width="320" height="475" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eliot Elisofon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Obafemi_Awolowo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
